# Everything here is excluded from the build context -- the set of files
# Docker uploads to the build engine before running the Dockerfile.
#
# Two reasons this file matters:
#
# 1. Speed. Without it, the entire directory ships to the daemon on every
#    build, including .venv and .git. That is tens of megabytes of pointless
#    copying per build.
#
# 2. Security. Anything in the build context can end up in the image, and
#    files added in one layer remain recoverable in image history even if a
#    later layer deletes them. A leaked .env is permanent.

.git
.gitignore
.github

.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
tests

# Secrets. Never in an image.
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json

README.md
GLOSSARY.md
docs
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
.DS_Store
